  "observations": {
    "territory": "Measured source front is substantially closer than previous straight western band. Complementary Orange/Purple ownership and new bright Purple gain are obvious. Front has residual angular steps and misses source micro-undulations, especially around occluded badge support and 64 uniform field knots. Thin existing/gained Purple material seam remains but is comparable in purpose to source.",
    "camera": "Original initial ~11-degree clockwise orientation and measured relative pan/zoom/rotation are now present. North/coast landmarks match far more closely; no black corners. Static landmarks were registered at mask IoU .953669, not pixel equality. Motion must still be inspected in all150frames.",
    "map": "Olive land and teal ocean palette are substantially closer; terrain texture is still visibly softer/coarser than reference relief. Existing simplified coastline differs visibly in western inlets/islands. No source screen bitmap copied. Native cartographic data does not justify texture parity.",
    "combat": "Eight correctly grouped polygonal soldier/flag badges are visible, mobile readable, and close to measured reference positions. Source sprite artwork is not identical: new authored icons have simplified blank faces/helmet/flag detail. No aircraft, nuclear symbol or explosion added. Three static frames do not verify all contact-cue timing.",
    "color": "Orange, existing Purple and brighter gained Purple are strongly distinguished; no decorative arrow, route trace or added frontier stroke is visible. Gained Purple is nearly opaque as in the source. Source and output composited RGB remain somewhat different.",
    "technical": "All three actual views are coherent, without black corners, detached overlay drift, gross rectangular mask or critical badge collision. Source preservation/GL status refer to actual probe evidence, not new independent source audit."
  },
